  "scope": "Ordinary memory and SQLite cancellation policy over unchanged native validation, bounded codecs, storage writes, group finalization and transaction ownership.",
  "limitations": [
    "Frozen policy shares native storage, input codecs/admission and group-finalization primitives, not the extracted ordinary cancellation orchestration.",
    "Disposable corrupt SQLite fixtures restore constraints before invoking the production transaction. They are not valid recovery checkpoints.",
    "The internal memory primitive retains missing-dispatch finalization and terminal replacement. The public VM entry still owns authority and replay; native memory mutations are not rolled back on later finalization failure.",
    "Ordinary durable replay retains original terminal validation, not new image/terminal correspondence. Unknown non-completed raw states retain their original write branch, not new recovery admission.",
    "Quota hook errors and uncertain commit/unwind are modeled directly; SQLite trigger and deferred-constraint failures exercise real rollback. No physical disk-full or power-loss experiment is claimed.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, standalone exported-source execution, complete host-neutral durable recovery or throughput benchmark is claimed."
  ],
